sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credit: the Pass 3 Koiter/FvK surface is a genuine reduced shell model — bilaplacian bending, varix pre-compression P(t) along s, Winkler foundation K_0 = (k_1^*)^4 from the Moulton-Chirat law, cubic saturation, and additive cord ridge forcing — relaxed from band-limited noise so the spine count (17 free vs theory 16.47; 16 when cord-locked) and the cord registration are emergent, not seeded (L670-900); the Mathieu k_c/2 pumping argument for rejecting stiffness modulation (L744-748) is correct physics; the graded-rigidity comb D(s) = (h/h_bar)^3 with local P_c(s) reproduces the WKB spacing law (L1047-1148); the instar scaling N_1 ∝ L^(1-3 beta/4) is exact (L1151-1190) and both laws are machine-checked (Lean Laws 4-5). Deductions: the Pass 2 1-D comb is not an emergent solver — the foundation is built from the rounded mode q_mode = 2 pi round(L/lambda_1)/L and the initial guess is the 16-mode itself (L230-263), so N = 16 is prescribed (-3); the \"Kirchhoff-Clebsch elastica\" does not integrate the ODE at L43-44, it draws a parametric omega loop with a linear neck-gap law and an uncited height law 4.8 sqrt(gamma - gamma_c) (L364-375) (-3); the frond cascade and the 120 deg varix cycle are prescribed cosines and bursts (L411-417, L457-462), only the k-ratios come from the model (-2); the Koiter model is linearised on a flat torus with nondimensional D = 1 but mm-labelled outputs, and the elastica cross-section is not coupled to it (-2); K_s = 0.48 for the frond cascade vs K_s_eff = 1.98 for the comb/Koiter solvers are two different foundation stiffnesses for the same law (L163, L213, L677) (-1); Pass 2 credited 93 for solvers that this pass shows were templated, so the dimension falls." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L230–L263: 1-D comb foundation k_sub = q_mode^4 with q_mode = 2 pi round(L/lambda_1)/L and 16-mode seeded init: spine count 16 is prescribed, theory gives 16.47 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L230-L263>",
            "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L364–L375: Elastica is a parametric omega loop (cos^1.8 profile) with linear neck gap and height 4.8 sqrt(gamma-gamma_c); the ODE in the header (L43-44) is not integrated <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L364-L375>",
            "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L411–L417: Frond stages are hand-drawn cosines; only k2_ratio / k3_ratio come from the wavenumber law <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L411-L417>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity-3> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.88"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity-1> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L670–L900" ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 reduced Koiter/FvK surface: bilaplacian + P(t) w_ss + K_0 w + kappa_3 w^3 - f_cord, varix tanh window (L727-731), cord ridge forcing with Mathieu justification (L744-748), noise init + gradient flow + L-BFGS-B, emergent count / registration / tilt (L835-865)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L670-L900> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity-2> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L1047–L1190" ;
        dct:description "Graded-rigidity comb D(s)=(h/h_bar)^3 with local P_c(s) and uniform control; allometric instar series with Brent root beta* = 4/3" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L1047-L1190> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity-3> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_077_mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling.lean L127–L188" ;
        dct:description "Laws 4-5: cord/varix intersection count = free spine count when lambda_c cos_den = lambda_1 cos_num; spine-count exponent 4 - 3 beta vanishes iff beta = 4/3; 0 sorry" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_077_mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling.lean#L127-L188> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Pass 3 remediated assessment, Phase B audit agent)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

